{"name":"Tretinoin for scalp","deep":true,"image":null,"mentions":26,"casual":{"lead":["Tretinoin is an approved acne and anti-aging retinoid. Hair-loss users mix it into minoxidil, or apply it to the scalp, hoping for better minoxidil absorption and more regrowth and density.","The proposed idea is that tretinoin helps minoxidil convert to its active sulfate form and penetrate the scalp. Reference sources describe the evidence for this use as weak and contradictory."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["It is used off-label, typically combined with a minoxidil solution applied to thinning areas as part of a daily routine. Users generally expect months before judging results."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["Irritation, peeling and sun sensitivity are common; oral forms carry pregnancy warnings. One case report describes scalp infection with a combination lotion."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[],"links":{"studies":[{"title":"Kerion Celsi favored by the use of a tretinoin+minoxidil+betamethasone valerate lotion in a 28-year-old woman.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20467404/","source":"Giornale italiano di dermatologia e venereologia : organo ufficiale, Societa italiana di dermatologia e sifilografia","year":2010,"cites":0,"kind":null},{"title":"Drugs for acne.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38294764/","source":"The Medical letter on drugs and therapeutics","year":2024,"cites":null,"kind":null},{"title":"Drugs for acne.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33443492/","source":"The Medical letter on drugs and therapeutics","year":2020,"cites":null,"kind":null},{"title":"Schools of pharmacology: retinoid update.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17039662/","source":"Journal of drugs in dermatology : JDD","year":2006,"cites":null,"kind":"Review"},{"title":"Safety and efficacy of Tretin-X compared with Retin-A in patients with mild-to-severe acne vulgaris.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16687979/","source":"Skin