l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tretinoin"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Hair (scalp)","chain":["Tretinoin mixed with minoxidil","Better minoxidil absorption","More regrowth, denser hair"],"effect":"indirect","text":"Users mix tretinoin into minoxidil, believing it improves absorption and gives fuller regrowth and denser-looking hair. It is an approved acne retinoid used off-label here, working through the proposed step of better minoxidil activation and penetration. Reference sources describe the evidence for the hair use as weak and contradictory."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["Tretinoin (all-trans retinoic acid) is a topical retinoid approved for acne and widely studied for photoaging.[1] In hair-loss communities it is sometimes applied to the scalp or mixed with minoxidil on the theory that it improves minoxidil absorption.","Wikipedia describes the proposed idea as tretinoin helping minoxidil convert to its active sulfate form and penetrate the scalp, and characterises the evidence as weak and contradictory.[1]"],"infobox":[["Drug class","Retinoid"],["Routes","Topical (scalp use off-label)"],["Approved topical uses","Acne, photoaging[1]"],["Common effects","Irritation, redness, peeling[1]"]],"sections":[{"h":"Uses","paras":["Tretinoin has been explored as an adjunct for hair loss, mainly in combination with minoxidil.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Pharmacology","paras":[],"subs":[{"h":"Mechanism of action","paras":["In skin, tretinoin binds retinoic acid receptors in keratinocytes and normalises follicle keratinisation.[1] The proposed hair mechanism involves enhancing minoxidil sulfation and penetration.[1]"]}]},{"h":"Adverse effects","paras":["Topical use commonly causes irritation, redness, swelling, peeling and sun sensitivity; oral tretinoin is contraindicated in pregnancy.[1] A case report describes kerion celsi, a fungal scalp infection, in a woman using a tretinoin, minoxidil and betamethasone valerate lotion.[2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found for tretinoin scalp use in androgenetic alopecia in the sources used here, beyond the case report above.[2]"],"subs":[]}],"lore":{"intro":"Tretinoin is discussed as a minoxidil booster.","claims":[{"claim":"Adding tretinoin to minoxidil boosts absorption and results.","verdict":"unknown","note":""}]},"timeline":[],"refs":[{"title":"Tretinoin (Wikipedia)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tretinoin","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Kerion Celsi favored by the use of a tretinoin+minoxidil+betamethasone valerate lotion in a 28-year-old woman","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20467404/","source":"Giornale italiano di dermatologia e venereologia","year":2010,"type":"study"}],"studies":[{"title":"Kerion Celsi favored by the use of a tretinoin+minoxidil+betamethasone valerate lotion in a 28-year-old woman","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20467404/","source":"Giornale italiano di dermatologia e venereologia","year":2010,"kind":null}],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Discussion Retin-A on eyelids: risk of getting MGD or dry/red eyes?","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/retin-a-on-eyelids-risk-of-getting-mgd-or-dry-red-eyes.572036/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220920180953/https://looksmax.org/threads/retin-a-on-eyelids-risk-of-getting-mgd-or-dry-red-eyes.572036/"},{"title":"LifeFuel Retin A does burn fat on the face","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/retin-a-does-burn-fat-on-the-face.495707/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220513134223/https://looksmax.org/threads/retin-a-does-burn-fat-on-the-face.495707/"},{"title":"retin a since 22 and dutasteride + dermarolling since 25 (28 now)","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/retin-a-since-22-and-dutasteride-dermarolling-since-25-28-now.433290/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20211218203007/https://looksmax.org/threads/retin-a-since-22-and-dutasteride-dermarolli